Phoenix-RTOS: SDL's stock Wayland video driver, statically linked.

The PHOENIX cmake branch (sdl2-drm patch 0002) skips the generic UNIX host probes;
sdl2-drm patch 0006 added CheckEGL() + CheckKMSDRM(). This adds CheckWayland(): it
finds wayland-client, wayland-egl, wayland-cursor, egl and xkbcommon through
pkg-config of the cross prefixes the build points PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR at (never the
host's) and runs the host wayland-scanner on SDL's bundled protocol XML files.

 * SDL_WAYLAND_SHARED must be OFF (enforced): SDL_waylanddyn.c then binds the
   WAYLAND_wl_*/xkb_* symbols to the real functions instead of SDL_LoadObject().
 * SDL_WAYLAND_LIBDECOR must be OFF (enforced): libdecor loads its decoration
   plugins as shared objects. SDL then asks the compositor for server-side
   decorations (zxdg_decoration_manager_v1), which labwc and Weston draw.
 * HAVE_MEMFD_CREATE: libphoenix has none; the Wayland stack's compat library
   (tools/gpu-lane/weston-drm/compat, over shmsrv) provides it and every Wayland
   program links it. The build puts that compat include directory on the C flags.
 * The core protocol's interface tables come from libwayland-client.a: SDL's
   copy generated from its bundled wayland.xml would collide with it in a static
   link, so only SDL's generated header is kept.
 * src/core/unix (SDL_IOReady: the display fd poll) is built, as in the UNIX branch.

KMSDRM stays enabled: with no Wayland socket, wl_display_connect() fails and SDL's
video init falls through to KMSDRM, as on Linux.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1524,6 +1524,38 @@
     set(SDL_INPUT_PHOENIX 1)
     file(GLOB CORE_PHOENIX_SOURCES ${SDL2_SOURCE_DIR}/src/core/phoenix/*.c)
     list(APPEND SOURCE_FILES ${CORE_PHOENIX_SOURCES})
+
+    # SDL's stock Wayland driver, for windows on a Wayland desktop (labwc, Weston):
+    # xdg-shell toplevels, server-side decorations through xdg-decoration, wl_seat
+    # keyboard (xkbcommon) + pointer (relative pointer, pointer constraints), GL/GLES
+    # through Mesa's EGL wayland platform. Linked statically like everything else on
+    # Phoenix: SDL_WAYLAND_SHARED must be OFF, and libdecor (a shared-library plugin
+    # system) is not used. The KMSDRM driver above stays: without a Wayland socket
+    # wl_display_connect() fails and SDL falls through to KMSDRM.
+    if(SDL_WAYLAND)
+      if(SDL_WAYLAND_SHARED)
+        message_error("SDL_WAYLAND_SHARED must be OFF on Phoenix-RTOS (static linking only)")
+      endif()
+      if(SDL_WAYLAND_LIBDECOR)
+        message_error("SDL_WAYLAND_LIBDECOR must be OFF on Phoenix-RTOS (no shared-library plugins)")
+      endif()
+      CheckWayland()
+      if(NOT HAVE_WAYLAND)
+        message_error("Phoenix-RTOS Wayland needs wayland-client, wayland-egl, wayland-cursor, egl and xkbcommon from the cross prefixes (pkg-config)")
+      endif()
+      # The core protocol's interface tables (wl_display_interface, wl_surface_interface...)
+      # are defined by libwayland-client itself. With a shared libwayland SDL's own copy,
+      # generated from its bundled wayland.xml, stays private to libSDL2; linked statically
+      # the two collide, so only SDL's generated header is used (libwayland 1.24 >= SDL's XML).
+      list(REMOVE_ITEM SOURCE_FILES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/wayland-generated-protocols/wayland-protocol.c")
+      # SDL_IOReady() (the display fd poll of the Wayland event loop, frame-callback waits)
+      file(GLOB CORE_UNIX_SOURCES ${SDL2_SOURCE_DIR}/src/core/unix/*.c)
+      list(APPEND SOURCE_FILES ${CORE_UNIX_SOURCES})
+      # libphoenix has no memfd_create(): the Wayland stack's compat library (weston-drm
+      # wlphx-compat, over the shmsrv server) provides it, and every Wayland program links
+      # that library. With it, SDL's cursor pools are shared memory the compositor maps too.
+      set(HAVE_MEMFD_CREATE 1)
+    endif()
   endif()
 
 elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT RISCOS AND NOT HAIKU)
